  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Wildlife Without Borders-Western Hemisphere</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The goal of this project is to protect and conserve threatened ecosystems within the Papaloapan River watershed, while improving the living conditions of the local rural and indigenous communities in the area. Project activities include: 1) design and implementation of community management plans as part of a comprehensive micro-watershed conservation strategy; 2) strengthen the capacity of community groups to protect forests, and develop their water management and governance skills; 3) introduce agroforestry and other sustainable pilot projects to slow the advance of agricultural frontier in the area; 4) develop environmental awareness among children, youth, and adults; and 5) promote environmentally-sustainable alternatives such as wood saving stoves, backyard vegetable gardens, chicken coops, dry latrines, among others.</narrative>
  </description>
